{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/113693-experience-points-costs","id":113693,"title":"Experience Points Costs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-15T17:56:13-07:00","id":113693,"title":"Experience Points Costs","content":"Hello all,<br /> <br /> Don't know if its been asked and answered, but I just bought the Mummy book, if I recall correctly it said something about it being part of a &quot;step foward&quot; in the Storyteller system. I assumed it worked with the new experience rules with beats and no &quot;X times new dots&quot; costs... Well my assumptions are wrong. Is there any plan for a conversion for it to be in line with the new books coming out, since its a very recent line? Its pretty easy to do it for the basics, but for Affinities and Utterances I don't have any idea yet. Any official words on it?<br /> <br /> Thanks,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T18:17:17-07:00","id":113715,"title":"","content":"CAS, the games main dev and line overseer is on these forums now and then. I know he mentioned the GMC rules thing in a text interview on the main Onyx Path site about nearly a year ago. He might pop in here to give you more concrete answer then I can. <br /> <br /> In the meantime I do believe there was a fan effort to adapt Mummy to the God Machine ruleset. I think it has its own thread further down this forum (towards the bottom I believe). It lists the XP costs for all the Mummy specific things in terms of GMC experience costs. <br /> <br /> As for an official update to Mummy into GMC, as far as I know at current there are no plans to do so. Mummy currently has about another 5 books to come out (plus a Dark Era's contribution and a section in the upcoming Hunter book Mortal Remains) before even its original projected splats are all out. The devs have implied that there may be a couple of splat books after that as well. <br /> <br /> In general I don't see Mummy getting an official GMC system update anytime soon. Maybe in about 4 years?<br /> <br /> Going with the presumption that the Werewolf and Mage Chronicle books make enough money that Onyx Path can do &quot;limited line&quot; Chronicle books. In which case my estimate is still based on the presumption that we get two chronicle books a year, in the manner that we are getting Werewolf and Mage in 2014. Meaning Promethean and Changeling in 2015, Hunter and Giest in 2016 and Mummy in 2017.<br /> <br /> This is all pie in the sky at the moment though.<br /> <br /> An alternative is that the &quot;limited&quot; lines like Promethean, Changeling and Mummy will receive basic system updates as part of later splat books. This is the approach that appears to being applied to Hunter the Vigil. With the new book &quot;Mortal Remains&quot; containing at least a chapter on updating that games base rule set to be GMC. Considering Hunter is easily the most &quot;core friendly&quot; of the game lines however, I'm not sure this approach would work with the other games lines.<br /> <br /> I feel your pain man. After GMC came out and I looked at the rules and my local group did some house-ruling and alterations to suit our style of play I realized how much better the GMC system is to WoD 1.0. I love Mummy, but if anything turns me even slightly off the game its the outdated rule system it uses. Considering that Mummy is a game I feel would have really benefited from both the the Conditions system and GMC's new approach to the idea of a &quot;morality stat&quot;.<br /> <br /> So the long on short is we keep waiting and see. Fingers crossed for a &quot;Shaunkshen Chronicle&quot; or something (Sekhem Chronicle?) in 2017.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T18:32:24-07:00","id":113726,"title":"","content":"Heya Hawthorn,<br /> <br /> Thanks for the comprehensive response.<br /> <br /> I got the Demon PDF and loved it so much I got Blood and Smoke... &quot;I'm thinking GMC Rules rock!&quot; And &quot;I need to get the other line that works with it!&quot; Impulse buying made me not do the research I usually do before buying something. Was reading through Mummy and loving the splat and having great ideas, I even really liked the dwindling power deal... But when it got to the crunchy part... All I can say is disappointment. But its all good, gotta play with the hand you're dealt. Bought both the Core and Guildhalls at once, so I hope at least my dollars help the line go forward.<br /> <br /> Thanks again for taking your time to answer.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T19:06:00-07:00","id":113749,"title":"","content":"Good move buying Guildhalls with the Core, it really makes the Guilds actually make a whole hell of a lot more sense as institutions in the modern world. <br /> <br /> Yeah Mummy's crunch is a bit...awkward at times. Some of the dice pools and contested rolls are all over the place and some affinities are just...damn near game breaking (God Sight, Soul Sight). If we never got the GMC update I'd just say that it does interesting things with the 1.0 system. In the face of GMC though, it just kinda comes off as clunky in places.<br /> <br /> On the bright side its really easy to update certain portions of the game like the combat mechanics and extended actions rules without screwing things up or anything. I did that in my Mummy/Changeling Campaign and it worked fine.<br /> <br /> I applied the idea from Blood and Smoke that like Vampires Mummy's take bashing from all mundane sources of harm (only supernatural powers that expressly say Lethal or Agg damage, Fire and damage wrap around do other types off the bat). This makes Mummy's even tougher.<br /> <br /> No worries on the answer, like I said hopefully a writer of CAS will pop in and give a more official statement. I'll I've got is supposition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T01:21:35-07:00","id":209913,"title":"","content":"My question is not about conversing the xp cost to GMC ules, but i wonder why the Mummy book states, that attributes cost New Dots x4 instead of New Dots x5. Is the x4 modifier only for mummies and if yes, why is it cheaper for them to raise attributes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1206-reiben","name":"Reiben","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T01:47:52-07:00","id":209939,"title":"","content":"Because Mummies are awesome.<br /> <br /> Seriously though, I can't remember the reason but the devs came out and said it wasn't a typo when the question was raised in the Errata thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T17:19:04-07:00","id":210657,"title":"","content":"IIRC, the xp costs were tailored to reflect a) mummies are immortal and have had plenty of on the job training that they dont remember, and b) some traits are restricted by the Judges. For example, despite it being eliminated in GMC, I kept Memory's xp costs scaling to reflect how hard it is to climb the pyramid. I also gave mummies the bashin damage stuff that Blood n Smoke gave to vampires. I think Cults expecially need GMC rules-- i have created gmc style &quot;cult&quot; merits for every mummy's cult in my game, so that each cultist gets certain boosts and high priests can throw around supernatural merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}